  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`assets/skills/habeas/SKILL.md` is a bundled skill: it has `name`/`description` front matter and sits under `assets/skills`. So `requirements.cli.skill_conventions.workflow` applies to it. The requirement has two obligations: the workflow must come before any other section, and it must be ordered steps.\n\n- **Placement:** The H1 `# Habeas` is followed by a short intro paragraph. The first subsection, `section[Habeas]/section[Workflow]`, is `## Workflow`. The other sections come after it: Testing and coverage artifacts, Inspecting, Requirements/examples/definitions, References and Gotchas. The intro is the body of the H1, not a separate section, so no other section comes before the workflow. The other bundled skills I checked, such as `habeas-refactor/SKILL.md`, follow the same layout of a short intro, then `## Workflow`.\n- **Ordered steps:** The workflow is a numbered checklist, `- [ ] 1. Pick the skill…` and `- [ ] 2. Follow that skill…`. That is ordered steps.\n\nNo violation queries were listed for this site, and I found no gap.\n\nOne reading could object that the intro prose comes before the workflow. The requirement says \"before any other *section*\", so I did not read it as banning an H1 preamble.",
